# `vector256` Standalone Wire Specification

`vector256` serializes an ordered JSON array of 256-bit hashes. Unlike several
other standalone codecs, its payload retains the ordinary XRPL VL length
prefix:

```text
VL byte length of concatenated hashes || hash[0] || hash[1] || ...
```

Each hash contributes exactly 32 bytes, so the decoded VL length must be a
multiple of 32. The VL prefix counts bytes, not elements. An empty vector is
the single byte `00`. The enclosing field-ID header used inside an `STObject`
is not part of the standalone codec.

